{
  "id": "Compound::DB06637 - Gene::3790",
  "verbalization": "Dalfampridine is likely to interact with Kcns3 through a shared pathway involving delayed rectifier potassium channels. The evidence suggests that Dalfampridine binds to Kcna6, Kcnf1, or Kcnv2, all of which participate in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. This activity is then associated with Kcns3, indicating a potential mechanism where Dalfampridine influences the function of these channels, which in turn affects Kcns3. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The involvement of multiple potassium channel subunits highlights the complexity of the pathway and the need for further investigation into how Dalfampridine modulates these channels to impact Kcns3.",
